---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

// PackForge, the report product, runs as its own application at
// reports.salet.uk on a navy and metallic-sky identity. This page carries
// that identity rather than the site's ivory, so a visitor arrives at the
// product already recognising it. The scheme is scoped to .reports-page and
// touches nothing else on salet.uk.
const REPORTS_URL = 'https://reports.salet.uk';
const SAMPLE_LEGAL = `${REPORTS_URL}/sample/legal-pack`;
const SAMPLE_INTEL = `${REPORTS_URL}/sample/intelligence`;
---
<Base
  title="Property reports | Legal pack review and buyer intelligence | Salet"
  description="Upload an auction pack and get back what the documents actually say, with the page behind every finding. Or an address in, and the sold evidence out as a range. Free while we launch."
>
  <div class="reports-page">
    <header class="rp-hero">
      <div class="rp-wrap">
        <p class="rp-eyebrow">Salet Property Intelligence</p>
        <h1 class="rp-h1">The evidence, before you commit</h1>
        <p class="rp-lede">
          Two reports for buyers of UK property. One takes an address and reports what the sold
          evidence supports, as a range, with the area behind it. The other reads the legal pack and
          cites the page behind every finding. Both are free while we launch.
        </p>
        <p class="rp-samples">
          Read a full example first:
          <a href={SAMPLE_INTEL}>sample Buyer Intelligence Report</a>
          <span class="rp-dot">·</span>
          <a href={SAMPLE_LEGAL}>sample Legal Pack Review</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </header>

    <section class="rp-wrap rp-cards">
      <article class="rp-card" id="buyer-intelligence">
        <p class="rp-tag">01 · An address in, the evidence out</p>
        <h2>Buyer Intelligence Report</h2>
        <p>
          What recent sold prices support as a range, the comparable sales behind it, the stamp duty
          on both bases, the official energy certificate, what it lets for locally, and the area:
          planning applications, flood risk, crime by offence, named schools and licensed shared
          housing nearby.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every figure is a range. Every block states its source and the date it was pulled. Where a
          source returns nothing, the report says so rather than leaving it out.
        </p>
        <ul class="rp-list">
          <li>Stamp duty at both ends of the range, as your only home and as an additional dwelling</li>
          <li>Like-for-like sales: the true peers by type and size, as a cross-check</li>
          <li>Rent led by actual lettings near the address, not a whole-city average</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="rp-price">Free while we launch</p>
        <a class="rp-btn" href={`${REPORTS_URL}/intelligence`}>Run a report</a>
        <p class="rp-fine"><a href={SAMPLE_INTEL}>See a full sample report</a></p>
      </article>

      <article class="rp-card" id="legal-pack">
        <p class="rp-tag">02 · Documents in, findings out</p>
        <h2>Legal Pack Review</h2>
        <p>
          Upload an auction pack, a lease, a management pack or a TA6. We work through a named risk
          checklist and report what the documents say, with the document and the page behind every
          finding, graded by whether it changes the price, needs an answer before exchange, or is
          simply worth knowing.
        </p>
        <p>
          The part most reviews skip is the part that costs money: what the pack leaves out. Missing
          searches, absent service charge accounts and unanswered title questions are reported as
          gaps, each with the question to put to the solicitor or the auctioneer.
        </p>
        <ul class="rp-list">
          <li>Special conditions read clause by clause, because that is where costs move to the buyer</li>
          <li>Ground rent, lease term, service charge arrears and s20 notices, quoted with their figures</li>
          <li>Tenancies, covenants, searches and the full fee stack on top of the hammer price</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="rp-price">Free while we launch</p>
        <a class="rp-btn" href={`${REPORTS_URL}/legal-pack`}>Upload a legal pack</a>
        <p class="rp-fine"><a href={SAMPLE_LEGAL}>See a full sample report</a></p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="rp-wrap rp-note">
      <h3>What these reports do not do</h3>
      <p>
        They report evidence. They do not tell you what to offer, what to bid, or whether to buy. A
        legal pack review states what the documents say and is not legal advice: a solicitor must
        review the pack before exchange. A survey and your own viewing complete the picture on any
        property.
      </p>
      <p class="rp-fine">
        Already used the free tools? The reports run on the same engine as the
        <a href="/deal-check">deal check</a>, <a href="/price-check">price check</a> and
        <a href="/refurb-check">refurbishment calculator</a> on this site.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>

<style>
  /* The report product's identity: royal navy with a metallic sky gradient,
     matching reports.salet.uk exactly. Scoped to .reports-page so the rest of
     salet.uk keeps its ivory and green untouched. */
  .reports-page {
    --navy-900: #08152c;
    --navy-800: #0f2244;
    --navy-700: #17325f;
    --navy-600: #1f437c;
    --sky-500: #5b8fc9;
    --sky-400: #86b0dc;
    --sky-300: #aecbea;
    --sky-100: #e8f1fa;
    --rp-paper: #f4f8fc;
    --rp-ink: #0b1626;
    --rp-slate: #5b6b80;
    --rp-line: #d5e0ec;
    --gold: #c8a95e;

    background: var(--navy-900);
    color: var(--rp-ink);
  }

  .rp-wrap { max-width: 68rem; margin: 0 auto; padding-left: 1.5rem; padding-right: 1.5rem; }

  .rp-hero {
    background:
      radial-gradient(90% 160% at 85% -30%, rgba(174, 203, 234, 0.28) 0%, rgba(174, 203, 234, 0) 60%),
      linear-gradient(100deg, var(--navy-900) 0%, var(--navy-700) 58%, var(--navy-600) 100%);
    padding: 5rem 0 4.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }
  .rp-hero::after {
    content: "";
    position: absolute; left: 0; right: 0; bottom: 0; height: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--gold) 0%, var(--sky-400) 42%, transparent 100%);
  }
  .rp-eyebrow {
    font-size: 0.72rem; letter-spacing: 0.18em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--sky-400); font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .rp-h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 72;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 5vw, 3.4rem);
    line-height: 1.05; color: #fff; margin: 0 0 1.25rem; font-weight: 500;
  }
  .rp-lede { color: var(--sky-300); font-size: 1.15rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 42rem; margin: 0 0 1.5rem; }
  .rp-samples { color: var(--sky-300); font-size: 0.95rem; margin: 0; }
  .rp-samples a { color: var(--sky-400); font-weight: 600; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
  .rp-dot { opacity: 0.5; margin: 0 0.4rem; }

  .rp-cards { display: grid; gap: 1.75rem; padding-top: 4rem; padding-bottom: 1rem; }
  @media (min-width: 56rem) { .rp-cards { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }

  .rp-card {
    background: var(--rp-paper);
    border: 1px solid var(--rp-line);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--sky-500);
    padding: 2.25rem 2rem 2.5rem;
  }
  .rp-card h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-variation-settings: "opsz" 72;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    font-size: 1.7rem; line-height: 1.15; margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--rp-ink); font-weight: 500;
  }
  .rp-card p { color: var(--rp-slate); line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 1rem; }
  .rp-tag {
    font-size: 0.7rem; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--navy-600); font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }
  .rp-list { margin: 0 0 1.5rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .rp-list li {
    border-left: 2px solid var(--sky-500);
    padding: 0 0 0 0.9rem; margin: 0 0 0.65rem;
    color: var(--rp-slate); font-size: 0.95rem; line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .rp-price { font-weight: 700; color: var(--navy-700) !important; }
  .rp-btn {
    display: inline-block; background: var(--navy-700); color: #fff;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.5rem; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.2s;
  }
  .rp-btn:hover { background: var(--navy-600); }
  .rp-fine { font-size: 0.85rem; margin: 1rem 0 0 !important; }
  .rp-fine a { color: var(--navy-600); }

  .rp-note { padding-top: 2rem; padding-bottom: 5rem; }
  .rp-note h3 {
    font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.15rem;
    color: var(--sky-300); margin: 0 0 0.75rem; font-weight: 500;
  }
  .rp-note p { color: var(--sky-300); opacity: 0.85; line-height: 1.65; max-width: 46rem; }
  .rp-note .rp-fine a { color: var(--sky-400); }
</style>
